# SonarCloud constraints

SonarCloud runs on CI. Write code that already passes these checks.

When a fix introduces a Sonar or lint pattern that is not listed here, add a short bullet to this file. Put test-only patterns in `testing.mdc`. Skip a pattern that is already covered or that only applies to one call site.

- Keep cognitive complexity at or below 15. Extract a helper when a function nests loops, conditions, or boolean chains.
- Define a function at module scope when it does not use variables from the enclosing function.
- Alphabetical `sort` and `toSorted` must take a compare function that uses `String.localeCompare` (typescript:S2871). Do not call either with no comparer. Sort numbers with a numeric comparer.
- Do not pass `unknown` or `object` values to `String()`. Narrow with `typeof value === 'string'` first.
- Compare with `undefined` directly instead of `typeof x === 'undefined'` (typescript:S7741). Reserve `typeof` for a binding that may not exist, such as `window` during server render.
- Use `??` when the only fallback is `null` or `undefined`.
- Use `??=` when a missing value should be assigned before it is used. Do not check it and then assign it.
- Import snapshot types from `src/types/snapshot.ts`. Do not re-export them from the file that uses them.
- Do not use `Math.random()` for tokens, secrets, session ids, passwords, or nonces (typescript:S2245). Use `crypto.randomUUID()` or `crypto.getRandomValues()`. `Math.random()` is only acceptable for non-security values such as UI jitter or demo data.
- Prefer `Number` static methods and properties over the global equivalents (typescript:S7773): `Number.parseInt`, `Number.parseFloat`, `Number.isNaN`, `Number.isFinite`, `Number.NaN`, `Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY`, and `Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY`.
- Group digits consistently when a numeric literal uses separators (typescript:S7749). Decimal groups are 3 digits (`1_000_000`). Hex groups are an even length, such as 2 or 4 (`0x1000_0000`). Do not leave a short group such as `0x1_0000_0000`.
- Every `<label>` needs accessible text and an associated control (Web:S6853). Set `for` to the control `id`, or wrap the control. Text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby` must name the label.
- Every `<input>`, `<select>`, and `<textarea>` needs a label (Web:InputWithoutLabelCheck). Give the control an `id` and point a `<label for>` at it, wrap it in a `<label>`, or set `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby`.
- Do not set `aria-hidden="true"` on a focusable element (Web:S6825): links, buttons, inputs, selects, textareas, `contenteditable`, or anything with `tabindex` of 0 or more. Put `aria-hidden` on a decorative child, such as an icon, instead of the control.
- Keep regular expressions linear (typescript:S8786). Do not nest quantifiers or overlap alternatives that can match the same text, such as `(a+)+` or `(a|aa)+`. Use one quantifier or a negated character class.
- Use a collection's contents or do not create it (typescript:S4030). Do not build an array, set, or map that is never read. Use `forEach` or a loop for side effects, and keep the result of `map`, `filter`, `slice`, and `concat`.
- Deep-clone with `structuredClone`. Clone `toRaw(value)` when the value may be a Vue reactive proxy.
- Do not nest ternaries. Assign the inner choice to a const, then use that const.
- Use a `Set` and `.has()` when a collection only answers whether a value is present. Do not build an array and call `.includes()`.
- Do not write `...(value ?? {})` or `...(value || {})`. Object spread already ignores `null` and `undefined`.
- Prefer optional chaining (`value?.field`) over `value && value.field`.
- Import Node builtins with the `node:` prefix, such as `node:path` and `node:util`.
- Mark a class field `readonly` when nothing reassigns it.
- Do not `await` inside a loop. Sequence dependent steps by returning the next promise from `.then`, or from a recursive function.
- In an ES module entry script, use top-level `await` inside `try/catch`.
- Do not mark a function `async` when its body has no `await`. When the signature must return a `Promise`, return `Promise.resolve(value)` from a normal function.
- Do not `await` a value that is not a promise.
- Throw `TypeError` when a `typeof` check fails. Keep `Error` for other failures.
- Use `replaceAll` when every match should be replaced. `findLast` replaces `filter(...).pop()`.
- Prefer `.at(-1)` over `[array.length - 1]`. Use `.at(index)` for any other index counted from the end.
- Read a non-global regex match with `pattern.exec(value)`. Do not use `value.match(pattern)`.
- Read a `Blob` or `File` with `blob.text()`. Do not use `FileReader#readAsText()`.
- Use `else if` for mutually exclusive branches. Do not nest a second `if` inside the `else`.
- Give `aside`, `nav`, and `section` an `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. A decorative SVG with no text gets `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Keep a function to 7 parameters or fewer. Put related arguments on one object.
- Handle a returned promise: `await` it, use `void` when its rejection is already handled, or attach `.catch` on an entry point.
- An `eslint-disable` comment names the rule it disables.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
return typeof window.localStorage === 'undefined' ? null : window.localStorage
if (!target.context) {
    target.context = {}
}
return names.sort()
return names.toSorted()
const sessionId = Math.random().toString(36)
const port = parseInt(raw, 10)
const letters = /^(a+)+$/
names.map((name) => name.toLowerCase())
const scale = 0x1_0000_0000
const cloned = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(value))
const status = cached ? 'cached' : response.ok ? 'ok' : 'error'
const layoutIds = ids.filter((id) => keep(id))
layoutIds.includes(id)
const last = items[items.length - 1]
const callsite = line.match(/^at (.+)$/)

// ✅ GOOD
return window.localStorage ?? null
const context = (target.context ??= {})
return names.sort((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right))
return names.toSorted((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right))
const sessionId = crypto.randomUUID()
const port = Number.parseInt(raw, 10)
const letters = /^a+$/
const normalized = names.map((name) => name.toLowerCase())
const scale = 2 ** 32
const cloned = structuredClone(toRaw(value))
const responseStatus = response.ok ? 'ok' : 'error'
const status = cached ? 'cached' : responseStatus
const layoutIds = new Set(ids)
layoutIds.has(id)
const last = items.at(-1)
const callsite = /^at (.+)$/.exec(line)
```

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<label></label>
<label>Route</label>
<input type="text" />
<select></select>
<textarea></textarea>
<button type="button" aria-hidden="true">Close</button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<label for="route-filter">Route</label>
<input id="route-filter" type="text" />
<label for="span-type">Span type</label>
<select id="span-type"></select>
<label for="trace-notes">Notes</label>
<textarea id="trace-notes"></textarea>
<button type="button">
    <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
    Close
</button>
```
